notes=['# Wavefunctions review comments — 25 September 2026','','13 comments addressed. Twelve chapters read; ten revised, Intro and John Cage retained. Two native museum photographs enter the canonical text.','','## Encounter before explanation','','The unit circle was freezing after its finite build. Its lower semicircle was also below the museum floor, and the entrance wall obscured part of it. The map now opts into continued projection, raises this existing artifact by 1.7 m and moves it one empty cell inward, from (1,1) to (1,2). Other circle placements retain the held default. The native placed scene has 400 steps, overriding the script default of 200. The same 400 local step transforms remain after motion and configuration toggles. The graph moves with the circle as one artifact; its geometry is unchanged and its resemblance to a bridge remains no guarantee of a walking route.','','No new artifact or primary promotion was needed. Paired walking steps and Bernini’s separate wall voice return to the prose as supporting encounters. Companion writing was read as earlier thinking, not as proof of current behavior; in particular the older circle intent overstates traversal and universal reduction to rotation. Those companion files are preserved.','','Lucier’s room stays substantial. It has a distinct departure and a real textual return to the five amounts on the bench. Feedback passes the changed sound into another operation; the bench recalculates its sum from coefficients and phase. Holding phase makes restoration visible without claiming that scene travel preserved the previous instant.','','## Evidence and limits','','36 final native checks pass: circle 16, synthesis 11, lattice 9. All exit 0. Actual signal emissions verify the bench and lattice controls. Circle motion uses controlled production updates and photographs at supplied phases. The lattice comparison uses 120 production steps at 1/60 s. These are not headset, pointer/grab, microphone, comfort or performance acceptance. The room entry/return wiring was inspected; the full scene travel was not exercised.','','The synthesis load reports existing scalar_pointer.gd:32 failures assigning control_path to XRToolsInteractableHandle. The coefficient and button signal tests pass independently; the shared pointer adapter is not changed by this review, and its interaction remains an open runtime follow-up. Existing unrecognized UID and renderer/build warnings remain in logs. See engine-limitations.json. No clean-engine claim.','','Initial camera attempts, including an outside-wall view and a half-buried circle, are retained as diagnostics. The final photographs were inspected and show the full circle from the interior. An early probe syntax error was corrected. The first pre-change run reported 7/7 and a frozen point, but its output directory was overwritten before archival; the saved pre-change source remains the baseline. It is not counted in the 36 final checks.','','Sequence order, artifact roles, all other placements, all code excerpts and companion manuscripts remain. Canonical final.md and the current Wavefunctions capture are updated; frozen historical captures and the live museum bake/save are untouched. Reload the Unit Circle hall for its source placement and motion change.','','## Decisions','']
