css='body{margin:0;background:#f5f0e8;color:#28232c;font:18px/1.7 Georgia,serif}main{max-width:1160px;margin:auto;padding:38px 28px}h1{font-size:48px;line-height:1.12}h2{line-height:1.3}p{max-width:78ch}a{color:#705079}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figure{margin:28px 0}figcaption,small{font-size:15px}figcaption{padding:10px 0}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.pair figure{margin:0}details{border:1px solid #cdc5bd;padding:16px;margin:18px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:bold}.diffwrap{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:10px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}.diff{font:12px/1.45 monospace}.diff td{padding:4px}.diff_header{background:#e3ddd4}.diff_add{background:#d3e8d5}.diff_sub{background:#f1d3d2}.diff_chg{background:#f3e6ae}.reading{max-width:760px;margin:40px auto 80px}.reading h1{font-size:36px}.reading pre{overflow:auto;background:#e7e1d7;padding:20px;font-size:14px}section{border-top:1px solid #ccc;padding-top:30px;margin-top:40px}code{font-size:.86em}@media(max-width:700px){h1{font-size:34px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Wavefunctions — what a return keeps</title><style>'''+css+'''</style><main><p>Ada Research · 25 September 2026</p><h1>What a return keeps</h1><p>The point comes round again. The graph stays where it was made. Later, a voice returns carrying what the last passage through a room did to it. Repetition has acquired different bodies, and each keeps something different available.</p><nav><a href="#reading">Read the sequence</a><a href="#comparisons">Inside the museum</a><a href="/book-tasks/review?seq=wavefunctions">Review comments</a><a href="DECISIONS.md">Decisions and evidence</a></nav><h2 id="comparisons">A complete circle, still turning</h2><div class="pair"><figure><img src="circle-interior/circle-top.png" alt="The old circle placement with its lower half below the floor"><figcaption>During inspection: the lower half disappears into the floor. The entrance wall also conceals part of the figure.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="circle-clear/circle-top.png" alt="The whole circle visible above the floor inside the museum"><figcaption>Raised and moved one cell inward. Same artifact; the full circle is now available to follow. The camera also moves to face it directly.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="pair"><figure><img src="circle-clear/circle-right.png" alt="Point at the side of the circle"><figcaption>A side: horizontal offset reaches its extreme.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="circle-clear/circle-top.png" alt="Point at the top of the circle"><figcaption>A quarter-turn later: vertical offset reaches its extreme. Same camera; the retained graph does not grow again.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>Returning to the five amounts</h2><div class="pair"><figure><img src="synthesis/sum-fifth-raised.png" alt="Fifth coefficient raised while the sum is held"><figcaption>HOLD, then raise the fifth slider. The curve changes at a kept phase.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="synthesis/sum-returned.png" alt="Baseline restores the held sum"><figcaption>BASELINE restores the five amounts and the same held curve. It does not rewind the clock.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The Lucier passage remains. Its doorway and the journey back are made explicit, and the ending returns to the bench for a comparison the reader can try. A filtered recording becomes the next input; the bench calculates a sum afresh.</p><h2>Which button is waiting for you?</h2><div class="pair"><figure><img src="lattice-interior/pulse-coupled.png" alt="Coupled pulse and current button captions"><figcaption>PULSE with links present; neighbour peak after two supplied seconds.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="lattice-interior/pulse-independent.png" alt="The same pulse without coupling"><figcaption>INDEPENDENT from the same still beginning. The neighbour stays at rest.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The prose now names the caption visible before a press. Elsewhere, counting waits for COARSE; directions use visible landmarks; Bernini’s wall voice enters the writing; the paired sine/cosine steps return as a supporting encounter. A maker’s walking-check note becomes a question a visitor can consider from the floor.</p><details><summary>Scope and open runtime issue</summary><p>13 comments addressed; ten canonical chapters revised, two retained. Two unmodified native museum photographs enter the book. One existing artifact gains an optional motion mode and a clearer placement. Sequence order and primary roles stay intact.</p><p>36 final native checks pass across three halls. These test supplied control signals and production updates, not tracked hands, headset comfort, microphone input or the full room-return journey. The synthesis load also exposes an existing scalar-pointer control_path error; its shared adapter needs a separate repair. UID and renderer warnings remain. Full logs and limits are in the decisions.</p><p>Reload the Unit Circle hall for its new placement and continuing motion.</p></details><section id="decisions"><h2>Each review comment</h2><table>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</table></section><section id="reading"><h2>Wavefunctions, in order</h2><nav>'''+''.join(f'<a href="#{m}">{html.escape(m.replace("WaveFunctions_", "").replace("Wavefunctions_", "").replace("_"," "))}</a>' for m in maps)+'''</nav></section>'''+''.join(parts)+'</main></html>'
